@startuml fig-1-1-context
' Figure 1.1 — System context
!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Web User" as User
actor "Researcher" as Res

rectangle "Explainable Security\n& Privacy Analyst" as SYS #E8F0FE

cloud "Websites visited\nby the user" as Web
cloud "VirusTotal\nreputation service" as VT
database "PhishTank feed +\nbenign URL corpus" as Corpus

User --> SYS : opens popup,\nreads reasons,\nreviews history
Web --> SYS : observable browser behaviour\n(requests, redirects,\npermission prompts)
SYS --> User : verdict, risk percentage,\nranked plain-English reasons
SYS --> VT : registrable domain
VT --> SYS : age and vendor votes\n(never a trained feature;\nnarrowly gated into the\nfused score, ADR-017)
Corpus --> Res : labelled URLs
Res --> SYS : trained model artefact

note bottom of Web
  The system observes pages
  from inside the browser.
  It never fetches a suspect
  URL from the server side.
end note
@enduml
